  "domain": "The frozen direct-only comparison split by difference: each Mitsuba picture removes one difference (reference noise, scene visibility, principled against glTF BSDF, the split-sum model with exact albedo integrals). Margo pictures are the frozen ones; every row is an exact first-measured budget, with edge and flat sums (edges: frozen reference steps above 30 summed RGB levels). Re-captured 2026-11-24 (KB6016b): the script's GGX D now writes its denominator |n x m|^2 + a2 (n.m)^2; the expanded float32 form cancelled near the normal, so at the alpha floor 1e-3 the glTF and split-model albedo integrals came out 0.896 instead of 1 on the roughness-0 spheres. Margo pictures are the height-correlated G2 table's. Re-captured 2026-11-27 on scalar_rgb (KB-REF-DECOMP-CUDA1): the CUDA variant summed a pixel's samples in an order that is not fixed, so no rerun repeated its raw bytes; each picture is now the float64 mean, in chunk order, of 8 scalar renders of 128 samples with seeds seed*8+i.",
